DESCRIPTION
.in +5
.br
The card's clone node (/dev/net0, sys/NET.md) is a TCP socket.  Socket
opens it; bind, listen, connect and accept are the driver's ioctls;
read and write move the bytes.  There is no fd_set layer: select (2)
takes the descriptor mask it always has.
.sp
The calls are IPv4 and TCP only.  The card parks one connection per
listener and refuses further connections until it is accepted; it has
no half-close, no options and no name store.  shutdown and setsockopt
succeed and do nothing.  getpeername and getsockname answer from what
bind, connect and accept recorded in this process, not from the card.
.sp
accept returns a new descriptor and the listener keeps its own: the
library duplicates the listener and the driver turns the duplicate
into the connection.
.sp
inet_ntoa takes a pointer to the address, not the address by value:
this compiler will not pass a structure as a call argument.

.HEADING net_join
net_join is not a socket call.  One call puts the card on its network
for every socket the process holds (N_JOIN, sys/NET.md); a daemon does
it once, on one of its sockets, before binding.
.sp 2
